-- title:
--   Reduced norms of away-units are units away from r
-- statement:
--   Fix rational numbers $a,b$ and let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and is finitely generated. Let $r$ be a prime number and let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose ideal contains the image of $r$. Here `CosetGraph.awayUnits R v` is the subgroup of $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b])^\times$ consisting of those $\gamma$ such that, for every height-one prime $w \neq v$, the image of $\gamma$ under the map induced by $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \to \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w$ lies in the subgroup generated by the units $u$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w$ with both $u$ and $u^{-1}$ in the local box [`Submodule.localBox R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40). The assertion is a conjunction. First, for every $\gamma$ in this subgroup and every prime $p \neq r$, the $p$-adic valuation of the reduced norm $\mathrm{nrd}(\gamma) = \gamma_{\mathrm{re}}^2 - a\gamma_{I}^2 - b\gamma_{J}^2 + ab\gamma_{K}^2$ vanishes. Second, conversely, every $c \in \mathbb{Q}^\times$ whose $p$-adic valuation vanishes for all primes $p \neq r$ has its image under the scalar embedding $\mathbb{Q}^\times \to (\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b])^\times$ in `CosetGraph.awayUnits R v`.
--
--   This is the standard statement that the reduced norm of an $r$-unit of a quaternion order is a unit away from $r$ (so of the form $\pm r^k$), together with the converse that the rational scalars which are units away from $r$ do lie in the group of $r$-units. It feeds the normalisation of reduced norms in [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_nrd_mul_pow_eq_pow_of_mem_awayUnits`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.exists_nrd_mul_pow_eq_pow_of_mem_awayUnits) and, through it, the analysis of the coset graph used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraph_padicValRat_nrd_eq_zero_of_mem_awayUnits.lean

